Use EGL_ANDROID_native_fence_sync on HarmonyOS.

GLFence::IsGpuFenceSupported() was false on OHOS whatever the driver
offered: GLFenceAndroidNativeFenceSync, and gfx::GpuFence's wait and status
calls, were only built for Android, ChromeOS and Linux. The system EGL
under ANGLE's GLES backend has EGL_ANDROID_native_fence_sync, and
OzoneImageBacking needs gpu fences to share a native pixmap between GL and
WebGPU (Dawn's Vulkan device), so they are built here too, with libsync.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51, on top of
chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.

diff --git a/ui/gfx/BUILD.gn b/ui/gfx/BUILD.gn
index 7714756..5952852 100644
--- a/ui/gfx/BUILD.gn
+++ b/ui/gfx/BUILD.gn
@@ -640,7 +640,7 @@ source_set("memory_buffer_sources") {
     deps += [ "//build/config/linux/libdrm" ]
   }
 
-  if (is_linux || is_chromeos || is_android) {
+  if (is_linux || is_chromeos || is_android || is_ohos) {
     deps += [ "//third_party/libsync" ]
   }
 
